# Publish finished phases

When an implementation phase is finished and its tests pass, commit that phase and push it to the tracked remote.

- Commit only the files that belong to the finished phase. Do not commit secrets, `.env`, or credentials.
- Use a commit message that states why the phase exists.
- Push the current branch to its remote. Do not force-push.
- If the phase is not finished, or tests are failing, do not commit it.
